# Code style

## TypeScript

- `strict: true` always. No `any` unless paired with a `// eslint-disable-next-line` and a comment explaining why.
- Prefer `type` for unions and `interface` for object contracts that may be extended.
- Use the `@/*` import alias for project-internal imports (`@/components/ui/button`, `@/lib/utils`).

## React / Next

- Server Components by default. Add `"use client"` only when you need state, effects, or browser APIs.
- Prefer composition (small components) over prop explosions.
- Co-locate files: `app/<route>/page.tsx` + `app/<route>/_components/`.
- Use `<Link>` from `next/link` for in-app navigation, `<Image>` from `next/image` for images.

## Styling

- Tailwind v4 utility classes — no separate CSS files except `app/globals.css`.
- Use `cn()` from `@/lib/utils` to merge classes:

  ```tsx
  import { cn } from "@/lib/utils";

  <button className={cn("px-4 py-2", isActive && "bg-primary text-primary-foreground")} />
  ```

- Prefer shadcn primitives (`@/components/ui/*`) over hand-rolled equivalents.

## Anti-patterns

- No default exports for utilities — only for Next route files (`page.tsx`, `layout.tsx`, etc.).
- No inline `style={{}}` unless the value is dynamic and can't be expressed in Tailwind.
- No `useEffect` for fetching in Server Components — fetch directly.
